From df9aaa298469079c6070f5f8fc1a1743190991a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeff Daily <jeff.daily@amd.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 03:46:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [ROCm] Document the AMD GPU build alongside the CUDA one

The HIP device backend added in the previous commit was not mentioned
anywhere a user looks for build instructions. This adds it in the two
places GooFit already documents its CUDA build: the requirements list and
the backend-selection section of README.md, and the per-platform build
recipes in docs/SYSTEM_INSTALL.md. The wording follows the existing
collapsible-section style rather than introducing a separate document.

The HIP device is never selected by GOOFIT_DEVICE=Auto, so the docs name
it explicitly together with CMAKE_HIP_ARCHITECTURES and the
GOOFIT_PHYSICS=OFF that the not-yet-ported amplitude-analysis PDFs
currently require.

No build or source file changes.

Authored with the assistance of Claude (Anthropic).

Test Plan:
```
# Radeon RX 7900 XTX (gfx1100), ROCm 7.2.5
cmake -S . -B build-hip -GNinja -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=RelWithDebInfo \
  -DGOOFIT_DEVICE=HIP -DCMAKE_HIP_ARCHITECTURES=gfx1100 \
  -DGOOFIT_TESTS=ON -DGOOFIT_EXAMPLES=ON -DGOOFIT_CERNROOT=OFF \
  -DGOOFIT_PYTHON=OFF -DGOOFIT_PHYSICS=OFF
cmake --build build-hip -j32
ctest --test-dir build-hip --output-on-failure
```

All 24 tests pass. The unbinned maximum-likelihood fit in the exponential
example recovers alpha = -1.001102381 +/- 0.003165763921 against a
generated value of -1, inside the tolerance the example itself asserts,
and repeats bit-identically over ten runs.
